---
title: Create a Vonage Application
description: Create a Vonage application in the dashboard and download the private key required by the backend.
---

# Create a Vonage Application

The Vonage Video API backend requires two credentials:

- **Application ID** – uniquely identifies your Vonage application.
- **Private Key** – used to sign JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) that authenticate API requests.

Follow the steps below to obtain both.

## 1. Sign in to the Vonage API Dashboard

Go to [https://dashboard.vonage.com](https://dashboard.vonage.com) and sign in with your Vonage account. If you do not have an account yet, [sign up for free](https://dashboard.vonage.com/?utm_source=DEV_REL&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=vonage-video-react-app) — new accounts include free credit.

## 2. Navigate to Applications

From the main dashboard menu, open the **Applications** section:

> **Dashboard → Applications**

You will see a list of existing applications, or an empty state if this is your first time.

## 3. Create a new application

Click **Create a new application** and fill in the form:

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Application name** | Choose any descriptive name, for example `vera-local` |
| **Public / Private keys** | Click **Generate public and private key** — the private key (`private.key`) will download automatically to your machine. Keep it safe. |
| **Capabilities → Video** | Toggle **Video** to the **on** position |

Click **Generate new application** to save.

## 4. Note your Application ID

After saving, the dashboard displays your new application. Copy the **Application ID** (a UUID that looks like `xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx`) — you will need it in the next step.

> **Where to find it:** The Application ID appears in the application detail page and also in the URL:
> `https://dashboard.vonage.com/applications/<your-application-id>`

---

You now have:

- ✅ A **Vonage Application ID**
- ✅ A **private key file** (`private.key`) downloaded to your machine

In the next step you will add these credentials to the backend environment file.
